<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">James Madison</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1751">1751</a>–<a href="/years/1836">1836</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">James Madison was the fourth president of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, from 1809 to 1817, and a principal author of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constitution-of-the-united-states">US Constitution</a> and the Bill of Rights. With <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-hamilton">Alexander Hamilton</a> and John Jay he wrote The Federalist essays in defence of the Constitution. As president he annexed part of Spanish West <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a> in 1810 and led the country in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-1812">War of 1812</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/james-madison.jpg" alt="James Madison" width="320" height="390" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: John Vanderlyn · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:James_Madison.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
